# AI coding workstation setup (Windows, macOS, Linux)

Instructions for a coding agent (Claude Code or Codex) to set up a machine to
match a reference workstation as of 2026-10-06. This document describes the
**target state, exact values and checks**. The agent chooses the commands for
the host OS and shell.

## How to use

1. Install Git and Claude Code or Codex, and log in.
2. Start the agent anywhere and paste:

```text
Set up this machine by following the instructions below. Detect the OS, CPU
architecture and shell first, and use that platform's normal commands. Work
through the sections in order. After each section, run its checks; if a check
fails and the fix is not obvious and safe, stop and show me the output. Back up
every existing config file before changing it, and merge — never replace —
existing settings. Ask me before anything that needs admin/sudo, a login, or
changes inside a project repository. Ask me which Git repositories to index.
Finish with the report in section 11.

<paste the rest of this document>
```

## Ground rules for the agent

- **Merge, don't overwrite.** Each user config may already hold other servers,
  hooks, permissions or instructions. Back up each file first (for example to
  `~/ai-setup-backups/<timestamp>/`). Then add or update only the entries named
  here.
- **Don't substitute.** If an exact version or option is unavailable, stop and
  report it. Do not pick a different version or an unfiltered alternative.
- **Never run these.** Each writes its own competing configuration:
  - `code-review-graph install`
  - `codebase-memory-mcp install` or `uninstall`
  - `serena setup` or `serena-hooks`
  - `context-mode`, ECC, or any `/plugin install` for these tools
  - the skills bundle's `/install-commit-gate`
- **No credentials in chat or logs.** The user does every login themselves.
- **Installing is not verifying.** A server is set up only when a fresh
  session lists it and answers a real call.

## Paths by platform

`~` means the user's home folder (`%USERPROFILE%` on Windows).

| Item | Windows | macOS | Linux |
|---|---|---|---|
| uv tool executables | `~\.local\bin\*.exe` | `~/.local/bin/` | `~/.local/bin/` |
| codebase-memory-mcp binary | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\codebase-memory-mcp\codebase-memory-mcp.exe` | `~/.local/bin/codebase-memory-mcp` | `~/.local/bin/codebase-memory-mcp` |
| Serena config | `~/.serena/serena_config.yml`, `~/.serena/contexts/` | same | same |
| Claude Code | `~/.claude.json` (user MCP servers), `~/.claude/settings.json`, `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` | same | same |
| Codex | `~/.codex/config.toml`, `~/.codex/hooks.json`, `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` | same | same |
| VS Code user `mcp.json` | `%APPDATA%\Code\User\` | `~/Library/Application Support/Code/User/` | `~/.config/Code/User/` |

Always register servers with **absolute executable paths**. Resolve them with
`uv tool dir --bin`, `which` or `Get-Command`; do not assume them.

